---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { GA_MEASUREMENT_ID } from '../site-config';
const updated = 'August 25, 2026';
const hasGA = Boolean(GA_MEASUREMENT_ID);
const CONTACT = 'support@sisrallc.com';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Wellness Med Care collects, why, and how to opt out. We do not collect health information."
>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:2.5rem">
    <div class="prose prose-center">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        We do not ask for, collect, or store health information about you. We do not sell
        personal information. The only personal information you can give us is an email
        address, typed into the newsletter box on purpose - and, like most websites, our
        host and analytics record standard technical data such as IP address and pages
        visited, described below.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> If you subscribe to the newsletter, your
      email address goes directly to our email service provider, which stores it on our
      behalf. If you email us, we receive what you send. That is it.</p>
      <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, our host
      and analytics record standard technical data: IP address, browser and device type,
      referring page, and the pages you visit. We use this to understand which guides are
      useful, not to build a profile of you.</p>
      <p><strong>Information we do not collect.</strong> We do not ask for your name,
      address, phone number, date of birth, Social Security number, insurance member ID,
      diagnoses, medications, or any other health information. Our tools that involve
      numbers run entirely in your browser - the values you type are not transmitted
      to us or stored on our servers.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies and similar technologies for basic site function and analytics. We
        intend to display third-party advertising, including Google AdSense, once the site
        is eligible. Advertising partners may set their own cookies and may use them to
        show ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of personalized Google advertising through
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">Google Ad Settings</a>,
        and out of many other vendors at
        <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">optout.aboutads.info</a>.
        Where required by law, we ask for your consent before setting non-essential cookies,
        and you can change that choice at any time through the cookie banner.
      </p>
      {hasGA && (
        <p>
          Google Analytics runs on this site only if you allowed it. No request is made
          to Google until you accept, and declining is remembered.
          <button type="button" data-reset-analytics class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-left:.5rem;font-size:.85rem;padding:.3rem .7rem">
            Change my analytics choice
          </button>
        </p>
      )}
      <p>
        We deliberately do not place advertising or analytics identifiers on pages in a way
        that would associate you with a specific medical condition.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To send the newsletter you asked for, and nothing else</li>
        <li>To measure which content is read, so we know what to write next</li>
        <li>To keep the site secure and working</li>
        <li>To comply with law</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not share it with lead
        buyers, insurers, providers, or data brokers. We share limited data with service
        providers who operate the site on our behalf - our host, our analytics
        provider, our email provider, and our advertising partner - and only so they
        can perform those services. We may disclose information if required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Every newsletter has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing deletes your address
        from our list. Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access,
        correct, delete, or port your personal information, to opt out of sale or sharing
        and targeted advertising, and to be free from discrimination for exercising those
        rights. We honor the Global Privacy Control signal as an opt-out of sale and
        sharing. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information
        from anyone under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and retention</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable safeguards to protect the little information we hold, and we keep
        email addresses only for as long as you stay subscribed. No method of transmission
        over the internet is completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will update the date above and, for significant changes,
        say so on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
